    "explanation": "This ruling concerns trip TRP-02704 of 29 August 2026 and the SGD 4.00 no-show fee charged on it. To both parties, in plain terms:\n\nTHE FEE STANDS. Under POL-NS-01 a no-show fee is chargeable only if all four conditions hold, and all four do. (a) The trip record carries the driver's 'I'm Here' arrival event at 21:58:18. (b) The driver's GPS trace (EV-GPS-02704, weight 1.0) places him inside the 50 m STANDARD arrival radius at 21:58:18 — the very timestamp of that event — with 46 fixes passing the 25 m accuracy filter. (c) He then held position inside that geofence continuously for 454 seconds, from 21:58:18 to 22:05:52, against the 300-second free waiting period recorded in the platform_policy in force for this trip; that is 154 seconds more than the minimum, measured from the first qualifying in-geofence fix as the clause requires. (d) No boarding event is recorded, and the driver terminated the trip at 22:05:55 under reason code RIDER_NO_SHOW, after the required dwell had elapsed.\n\nTO THE RIDER: your claim that the driver 'cancelled on me while I was walking to the bay' is not supported by the record. Your own device's GPS track shows you stationary at 0.0 km/h at roughly 606–613 m from the pickup pin across the whole window, with not one qualifying fix inside the 100 m rider-presence radius. You did not answer the driver's 21:58:48 message ('I am at the bay, which door are you at'), which you read at 21:59:38, before the 22:05:55 cancellation. POL-NS-04 therefore cannot exonerate you: its limb (a) fails because you sent no locating or coordinating message, and its limb (c) is affirmatively failed on admissible fixes. POL-NS-05 gives you nothing either — at the arrival timestamp the trace shows the driver stationary inside the geofence and not moving at 15 km/h or more, so the arrival marker was not false and the waiting clock stands as tapped.\n\nTO THE DRIVER: the SGD 4.00 fee is upheld and you are paid SGD 3.20. The fare ledger line of SGD 4.00 (EV-FARE-02704, weight 1.0) reconciles with the platform_policy cancellation fee of SGD 4.00 for this trip, so there is no fare-integrity defect. The POL-NS-07 anti-farming check does not trip: driver_profile.no_show_terminations_30d is 2, below the required 4, and 2 against 111 completed trips in 30 days is a ratio of 0.018, below the 0.08 rate. You therefore receive 80% of the SGD 4.00 fee, i.e. SGD 3.20; the residual SGD 0.80 is the platform's service fee. The disposition of the fee itself is NO_ACTION (the charge stands as it presently is); the ruling value is DRIVER_COMPENSATION because that is the outcome the case produces, and amount_sgd mirrors driver_compensation_sgd per POL-GEN-03.\n\nTHE MISSING ADVISORY PLAYS NO PART. EV-ADVIS-02704-01 is MISSING with weight 0.0 and issue MISSING_ARTIFACT. It is not relied on: the driver's single continuous 454-second in-geofence run already exceeds the 300-second minimum, so the POL-NS-06(i) accumulation route the absent advisory would have unlocked is unnecessary. Two claims that asserted that route without disclosing the advisory's impairment were discarded in the audit below.\n\nNO ESCALATION. No admissible artifacts contradict each other on arrival, dwell or rider presence; neither profile shows 2 or more no-show disputes between these parties in the trailing 90 days (both 0); rider_profile.no_show_disputes_30d is 0, not 3 or more; the anti-farming check does not trip; and no deciding fact rests solely on impaired evidence. Confidence is 0.90, above the 0.70 floor — the cap is 1.0 because every artifact carrying a deciding fact (the driver's GPS trace, the trip record and the fare ledger) has weight 1.0. No clause produces a referral, so referrals is empty. The monetary effect of SGD 3.20 is below the SGD 8.00 execution threshold, so it executes on issue. This ruling was made without human review; either party may appeal it once within 30 days under POL-GEN-04."
